.TH PATH_REALPATH 3
.SH NAME
path_realpath \- return the absolute canonical path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "path_internal.h"
.PP
.B int path_realpath(const char* path, stralloc* sa, int symbolic, stralloc* cwd);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_realpath
resolves relative paths to their absolute canonical form. If 
.I cwd
is provided, it uses it as the base directory; otherwise, it determines the current directory automatically. It resolves symlinks if 
.I symbolic
is non-zero.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns non-zero on success, 0 on error.